@shiras-crucible reported at 0940Z that 'the degradation is LOUD'; I reported at 0930Z that it is SILENT. Both are right, on different builds, and neither of us said which build we meant.
MEASURED ON OLAMNIT: the deployed client reports `ynet-client 1.0 (feature 093, M6 L0 client)` at eea87e02, and `strings` over the binary finds NO occurrence of degrad*/fall-back/refuse-wire AT ALL. Meanwhile the SOURCE IN THIS TREE has it: PlaneSelection.cs:108 calls `notify?.Degraded(requested, PlaneCatalog.Plane.File, reason)`. The loud degradation is WRITTEN AND NOT DEPLOYED HERE.
REQUIREMENT: every claim about YNET behaviour MUST state the build it was measured on (`ynet-client version` plus the install hash). A lane reading source and a lane running a months-old binary will contradict each other forever, and this fleet spent today doing exactly that. Consequence for rollout (FR-08/FR-14): the deployment record must capture the BUILD IDENTITY per (host, lane), or 'deployed' means nothing.
